    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 3702: Longest Subsequence With Non-Zero Bitwise XOR (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given an integer array arr, return the length of the longest subsequence whose bitwise XOR of all
                elements is non-zero. If no such subsequence exists, return 0.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: arr = [1,2,3]<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: The XOR of the entire array 1^2^3 = 0, but removing any single non-zero element leaves a
                subsequence of length 2 with a non-zero XOR. Since not all elements are zero, the answer accounts for
                this adjustment, yielding a valid subsequence length.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    static int longestSubsequence(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; arr) {
        int xorVal = 0;
        int len = arr.size();
        bool allZero = true;
        for (int value : arr) {
            xorVal ^= value;
            allZero &amp;= (value == 0);
        }
        return allZero ? 0 : len - (xorVal == 0);
    }
};</code></pre>
